s":[],"isCrawlJob":false},"isViewed":false,"isActive":true},{"storyId":235595,"name":"Course Developer (Freelance) (Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostic for Chinese Medicine) (N&HS) (Ref: 260012Z)","createDate":"2026-05-13T12:02:39.274924","postDate":"2026-05-13T13:00:19.914821","article":null,"job":{"jobId":"10108370","jobTitle":"Course Developer (Freelance) (Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostic for Chinese Medicine) (N&HS) (Ref: 260012Z)","companyName":"Hong Kong Metropolitan University","companyLogo":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company/muhk-white_z.gif","companyBanner":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company_banner/jobdetails/hong-kong-metropolitan-university19.jpg","url":"https://jobs.ctgoodjobs.hk/job/10108370/course-developer-freelance-professional-diploma-in-advanced-diagnostic-for-chinese-medicine-nhs-ref-260012z","content":"<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the <strong>School of Nursing and Health Sciences:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><strong>Course Developer (Freelance) (Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostic for Chinese Medicine) (N&HS) (Ref: 260012Z)</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><strong>Programme Code: PDADCM</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Programme Title: Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostic for Chinese Medicine</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The appointee will support the development of the Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostic for Chinese Medicine for the School of Nursing and Health Sciences on a freelance, project-based basis. The programme will be developed in English.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><u><strong>Major Duties and Responsibilities</strong></u></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following:</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Developing of course proposal;</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Developing of PowerPoint presentations; and</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Preparing of teaching notes.</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><u><strong>Candidates</strong></u></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Candidates are expected to possess the following:</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">A higher degree in Health Sciences, or radiology and medical imaging;</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Teaching experience in a health-related discipline;</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Good command of written English;</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Preferably with experience in part-time courses; and</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Previous involvement in developing course materials for higher institutions is a definite advantage.</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><u><strong>Background</strong></u></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The Professional Diploma in Advanced Diagnostics for Chinese Medicine is designed to bridge the gap between Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) practice and modern diagnostic technologies. It equips TCM practitioners with a comprehensive \"Safety-Legal-Clinical\" framework, seamlessly integrating medical imaging, laboratory science, and medical law. Aligning strictly with the latest Chinese Medicine Council of Hong Kong (CMCHK) Referral Guidelines, the programme shifts the focus from merely \"treating\" to effective \"screening.\" It trains practitioners to identify life-threatening conditions, execute timely triage, and make evidence-based referral decisions. This clinician-centric approach fosters inter-professional collaboration and significantly enhances patient safety in primary care settings.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">This programme will cover the following topics:</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Medical Imaging Physics, Technology & Safety</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Imaging Anatomy</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Integrated Medical Image Interpretation</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Applied Laboratory Diagnosis</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Legal Risks & Medical Liability in TCM Practice</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Emergency Identification & Triage Practice</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Upon completion of this programme, students should be able to:</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">1. Demonstrate in‑depth specialised knowledge of medical imaging physics, cross‑sectional anatomy, and laboratory science, applying this knowledge to improve diagnostic accuracy in TCM practice.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">2. Critically analyse clinical indications, contraindications, and patient safety issues to formulate evidence‑based referral strategies for appropriate diagnostic tests.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">3. Interpret diagnostic imaging reports and laboratory data, synthesising them into integrated treatment plans that align modern diagnostic findings with TCM principles.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">4. Evaluate acute and urgent clinical presentations in an outpatient setting, applying structured triage procedures to execute timely emergency or specialist referrals.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">5. Critically evaluate professional risks, legal boundaries, and ethical responsibilities related to diagnostic referrals and inter‑professional collaboration, applying relevant guidelines in routine practice.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><u><strong>Terms and Conditions for Appointment</strong></u></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Successful candidate(s) will be appointed on a freelance basis.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">\u00A0</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><u><strong><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">To Apply</span></span></strong></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Please send your full curriculum vitae to the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, Hong Kong Metropolitan University by email at [via CTgoodjobs #Apply-Now-Email#]. Applicants should quote the reference number in the subject line of the application email.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Closing date of application: 27 May 2026</span></span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><em><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.\u00A0 For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful.</span></span></em></p>\r\n","applyUrl":"https://www.ctgoodjobs.hk/ctjob/apply/jobApply.asp?m_jobid=10108370","whatsappUrl":null,"highlights":[],"isCrawlJob":false},"isViewed":false,"isActive":true},{"storyId":235573,"name":"Clerk (<strong>part</strong>-<strong>time</strong>)","createDate":"2026-05-13T11:45:20.019571","postDate":"2026-05-13T13:00:19.914821","article":null,"job":{"jobId":"10108344","jobTitle":"Clerk (part-time)","companyName":"Phillip Securities Group","companyLogo":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company/phillip_securities_z.gif","companyBanner":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company_banner/jobdetails/phillip-securities-group.jpg","url":"https://jobs.ctgoodjobs.hk/job/10108344/clerk-part-time","content":"<p><strong>Position Overview:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>We are looking for a Part-time\u00A0Clerk to assist with data entry. This is an excellent opportunity for students or individuals seeking part-time or summer work experience in a professional office setting.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p>\r\n\r\