boratories, ensuring compliance with health and safety regulations; and<br />\r\n(c) To assist academic staff and provide technical support to students during practical classes, laboratory work and projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><u><strong>Requirements:</strong></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) A recognised Diploma or Higher Certificate, preferably a higher qualification, in Mechanical Engineering or a related discipline;<br />\r\n(b) Technical competency in one or more of the following areas: CNC machining, 3D printing, and robotic arm operation, including:<br />\r\n(i) At least two years of proven hands-on experience in operating a 4-axis CNC machine; and/or<br />\r\n(ii) Demonstrated proficiency in the operation and maintenance of 3D printers, with prior experience using the Voron series being an advantage; and/or<br />\r\n(iii) Practical experience in operating and maintaining a robotic arm (e.g., basic teaching/programming, calibration, and safety procedures), is preferred;<br />\r\n(c) At least 2 years’ relevant work experience, preferably in tertiary education institutions or comparable organisations;<br />\r\n(d) Preference will be given to candidates with hands-on experience in operating and maintaining digital manufacturing / prototyping equipment in a workshop or laboratory setting;<br />\r\n(e) Be responsible, safety-conscious, and able to document work clearly;<br />\r\n(f)\u00A0 Good communication and interpersonal skills; and<br />\r\n(g) Good command of English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><u><strong>Notes:</strong></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>(1)\u00A0 The appointee may be required to perform duties at different sites and work irregular hours, including Saturdays and Sundays as necessary.<br />\r\n(2) The remuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience.<br />\r\n(3) The appointee will work at the Tsing Yi Campus.</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><u><strong>Application Procedures:</strong></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">A completed application form<em><strong>\u00A0[THEi-HR-601 (Dec 2025)]</strong></em>, together with\u00A0<u>a full curriculum vitae</u>, should be sent to\u00A0thei-jobs@thei.edu.hk.\u00A0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Applicants should take note of the following:<br />\r\n(1) Completed application form and detailed curriculum vitae (CV) should be combined into\u00A0<u><strong>one file in PDF format with a file size below 10MB</strong></u>.<br />\r\n(2) The file should be saved with the applicant’s name as “surname and given name”, e.g. “CHAN Siu-lam.pdf”.<br />\r\n(3) For the email subject, please cite “Application for Part-time Technician, Digital Manufacturing, DCEE (Ref No.: DCEE/TECH(DM)/03/26)”.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Closing date for applications: 29 May 2026</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><em>The Institute reserves the right not to fill the post. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Information on unsuccessful candidates will normally be destroyed 12 months after the completion of the recruitment exercise.</em></p>\r\n","applyUrl":"https://www.ctgoodjobs.hk/english/count/count_job_detail.asp?job_id=10107559","whatsappUrl":null,"highlights":[],"isCrawlJob":false},"isViewed":false,"isActive":true},{"storyId":234369,"name":"<strong>PART</strong>-<strong>TIME</strong> CUSTOMER SERVICE AMBASSADOR (Hourly Rate: HK$85)","createDate":"2026-05-12T16:30:27.080004","postDate":"2026-05-13T13:00:19.914821","article":null,"job":{"jobId":"10107533","jobTitle":"PART-TIME CUSTOMER SERVICE AMBASSADOR (Hourly Rate: HK$85)","companyName":"Times Square Limited","companyLogo":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company/times_square_2_z.gif","companyBanner":"https://res04.ctgoodjobs.hk/images/company_banner/jobdetails/times-square-ltd.jpg","url":"https://jobs.ctgoodjobs.hk/job/10107533/part-time-customer-service-ambassador-hourly-rate-hk85","